model {
  extend basalt.router {
    metadata {
      constraint "On a disposable stage the Router alone serves the app host, through its custom domain and a zone route for that one host. Production's Router owns the zone's app-origin wildcard route, a zone route runs before a custom domain, and production's Router answers any host but its own with an empty 404, so without its own route a stage's app host reaches production's Router. The upstream role hosts give the API Worker no zone route and the stage no record for the app host when EXECUTOR_APP_HOST_ROUTER is set, which only Basalt's disposable stages do; the API keeps its mcp and api hosts. Production keeps its wildcard and its product-host bypass routes, and refuses the switch."
    }
  }
}
